# SafeEdge — Angular UI

Framework: Angular, standalone-first. Target: predictable, declarative, typed UI code.

SafeEdge is an internal analysis dashboard, not a public-site / admin-site split. Later screens may include Dashboard, Events, Markets, Candidates, Odds History, and Backtests. Do not invent a CMS, public theme skins, or an admin/public dual app unless a task asks for it.

## Components

- All components are standalone. Do not use NgModules for feature wiring.
- No inline templates or inline styles. Use separate `.html` and `.scss` files.
- `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` on components.
- Modern control flow only: `@if`, `@for`, `@switch`. Do not use `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`, `*ngSwitch` except when a third-party component requires it.
- No heavy logic in templates (no sorting, filtering, mapping, or betting math in HTML). Use `computed()` or pipes.

## State and async

- Prefer Angular Signals for local UI state and `computed()` for derived state.
- Comment `effect()` side effects.
- Keep state component- or service-scoped. Do not introduce NgRx, Akita, Elf, SignalStore, or a custom global store unless explicitly requested.
- RxJS for asynchronous/external streams. Convert to Signals in the UI layer with `toSignal()` or `async` when that is clearer.
- Every non-HTTP subscription must be cleaned up with `takeUntilDestroyed()` or `DestroyRef`.
- HTTP calls belong in services. Components orchestrate; services execute. No HTTP in templates or constructors.

## Forms and typing

- Prefer typed Reactive Forms.
- Validation belongs in validators, not duplicated in templates.
- No casual `any`. No `as unknown as` casts.
- Do not display raw enum values in templates. Use a shared label mapping when enums are shown; do not invent per-enum pipes.

## Time

Frontend is not the authoritative source of business time.

Do not compute "now", "today", kickoff remaining, snapshot age, closing-odds cutoff, or backtest windows in the browser except for purely visual formatting of values the backend already returned.

Allowed: date pickers as explicit user input, rendering backend timestamps, passing user-selected dates to the API.

Default business dates and "current time" come from the backend `Clock`.

## Generated OpenAPI

Do not hand-edit generated TypeScript clients/models. Change the spec or generator config and regenerate.

## Lists and layout

Fit tables/lists in the viewport. Prefer `table-layout: fixed` and ellipsis for overflow rather than horizontal scrolling.

Reuse shared page chrome (list layout, table surface, headers) instead of copying shell styles between screens.

Theming/tokens: see `ui-theming.mdc`.

## When uncertain

Stop and ask instead of copying a previous project's admin/public UI model.
